  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-agent-orchestrator — deprecated",
      "text": "> **This plugin is no longer maintained.** Multi-agent orchestration is built into\n> DeepSeek Harness since **0.1.5**. Remove the plugin and use the built-in tools below.\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web remove @goodandready/dsh-agent-orchestrator\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "What to use instead",
      "text": "| The plugin gave you | Built into DeepSeek Harness |\n|---|---|\n| Task decomposition, DAG pipelines, worker pool | the `workflow` tool — a JavaScript orchestration script that runs subagents in the sandbox, with run progress shown in the conversation |\n| Specialized roles (spec, backend, QA, docs…) | the `subagent` tool with `agentPreset` — any agent preset, including your own |\n| \"Keep going until it is done\" loops | the `ralph` tool — a loop of fresh agents over the workflow and subagent seams |\n| Agent teams, shared task board, agent mailbox | Agent Teams (experimental, DeepSeek Harness 0.1.7) |\n| `/orchestrate`, `/orc`, `agent_run` | ask the agent to use `workflow` or `subagent` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Data",
      "text": "The plugin kept its state in `~/.dsh/orchestrator-pipelines.json` and\n`~/.dsh/orchestrator-snapshots/`. After removing the plugin these files are no longer read\nand can be deleted."
    },
    {
      "section": "History",
      "text": "The last functional release is **0.1.12**. Version **0.1.13** only carries this notice;\nthe code is unchanged. See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).\n\nLicense: MIT."
    }
  ],
